<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Latvia partial election results put PM's pro-Ukraine party ahead but coalition partners stumble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec991fc1c3e5fb47e585f3d17c2c6ab9e3391e566e41428a5a5cf5059dc85d02</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T20:58:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-latvia-elections-pm-kulbergs-pro-ukraine-party-ahead-coalition-partners-stumble" /><summary type="html">Latvian Prime Minister Andris Kulbergs' pro-Ukraine and pro-Europe party was seen winning a parliamentary election on Saturday by an unexpectedly wide margin, partial results showed, even as projected results for other coalition parties suggested the centrist PM would have to form a new ruling coalition.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro make final push for votes ahead of Brazil's knife-edge election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c52683453d6d5e1a213d4e0941c87da4873392ef063f319b36e352322fcf0649</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T20:16:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-lula-and-bolsonaro-make-final-push-for-votes-ahead-of-brazil-s-knife-edge-election" /><summary type="html">Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his main challenger Flavio Bolsonaro wrapped up their campaigns on Saturday in the powerhouse state of Sao Paulo, where a fifth of the nation's vote is based, seeking to rally supporters and convince the undecided on the eve of Sunday's nail-biter election.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Putin's war for the history books: Dmytro Kuleba speaks to France 24</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35c3e5cadaa7738569f6cc76c0f01d4ec35ebb36d4ef35230f20861337ce7616</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T18:08:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261003-putin-s-war-for-the-history-books-dmytro-kuleba-speaks-to-france-24--8a38a0a2beb7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261003-putin-s-war-for-the-history-books-dmytro-kuleba-speaks-to-france-24" /><summary type="html">The Bronze Horseman, the iconic equestrian statue in Senate Square in St Petersburg, was commissioned by Catherine the Great in honor of Peter the Great, the city's founder. The pedestal of the statue bears a laconic dedication, "To Peter the First, Catherine the Second, 1782". Does Putin want to be the third, Vladimir the Great? And is that ambition, expansion at any cost, the real reason behind the war in Ukraine? According to Former Ukrainian Foreign Minister Dmytro Kuleba, "Putin only cares about what will be written about him in history books."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee prison chief who oversaw botched Christa Pike execution resigns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32be97bb42a3bf22876e69cdc90e198ce6a2a46f20c0e1e6f4b1ad8004f189d5</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T17:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-tennessee-prison-chief-who-oversaw-botched-christa-pike-execution-resigns--070a60d4707d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-tennessee-prison-chief-who-oversaw-botched-christa-pike-execution-resigns" /><summary type="html">The head of Tennessee's prison system has resigned in the first major shake-up since the stunning failed execution of Christa Pike, who is in critical condition after surviving two lethal injections. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee, who previously denied Pike clemency, has halted further executions through the rest of the year while a review is conducted.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Italy’s Ustica enigma: Can French files solve mystery crash blamed on stray missile?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c86443216ab2d5e7c3fed9e58341bc129f0d0705e80e66c9310063e27295b70</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T15:42:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-italy-ustica-enigma-can-french-files-solve-mystery-crash-blamed-on-stray-missile-gaddafi--dd128b356206.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-italy-ustica-enigma-can-french-files-solve-mystery-crash-blamed-on-stray-missile-gaddafi" /><summary type="html">France’s decision to share defence documents with the Italian judiciary has raised hopes of a breakthrough in investigations into the 1980 crash of a passenger jet near the island of Ustica, which a former Italian president claimed was mistakenly shot down by a French fighter jet. Sceptics caution that the files are unlikely to shed light on one of Italy’s most enduring mysteries, let alone reveal a culprit.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim strike on oil facilty near Riyadh, accuse Saudi forces of pounding Yemen's capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7182d0a7242c2d9060b3891ee07a86ecc9c0b4fc8c07f33bd3c552e8570909b</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T14:31:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa--81b4ce29f4be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa" /><summary type="html">Houthi rebels accused Saudi forces of launching 26 strikes on Sanaa on Saturday after loud explosions rocked the Yemeni capital. The Iran-backed group said it struck an oil facility south of Riyadh, where flames and a large plume of smoke were seen rising from a plant belonging to oil giant Aramco.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Fresh protests over housing flare in Spain after lawmakers reject relief measures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ceacf4758186d65c0224b8d60bd4dc27d390ad764771385bc1645c72ce72a8f2</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T13:20:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures--704e7b8d4986.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters marched in Madrid and other cities in Spain on Saturday to demand affordable housing, fuelled by anger at lawmakers who narrowly rejected measures put forward by the government of Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to strengthen protection for tenants.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro: In the name of the father, sons, and holy ideology</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea01a4ea7b312946b4c9d4188978b71cb809d59481857c62c23d906a70c5c23a</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T09:48:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-flavio-bolsonaro-in-the-name-of-the-father-sons-and-holy-ideology--9892326d1899.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-flavio-bolsonaro-in-the-name-of-the-father-sons-and-holy-ideology" /><summary type="html">The first round of Brazil’s presidential election on Sunday pits two well-known names in the political ring: Lula vs. Bolsonaro. But it’s not former president Jair Bolsonaro facing off against the incumbent head of state – it’s his eldest son, Flavio Bolsonaro. He’s less charismatic than his father but just as ideologically radical as the family patriarch.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Barricades &amp; the blame game: the French school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:772478e3841653936c111a837ae80fe9d4e8b3274c332b14fa6a4e3e6fd9b269</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T09:25:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261003-barricades-the-blame-game-the-french-school-protests--b90ad964f1c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261003-barricades-the-blame-game-the-french-school-protests" /><summary type="html">In a week that’s seen the heroism of the captain, crew and passengers on board FlyDubai flight 1073 heralded, eye witnesses report seeing the co-pilot trying to kill the pilot and destroying the cockpit controls in order to crash the plane. Despite being stabbed repeatedly, Captan Smit Machchhar managed to open the cockpit door, allowing passengers to overwhelm the suspect and regain control of the aircraft after its rapid descent of more than 14,000 feet in 30 seconds. They prevented a 9/11-style catastrophe, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>No fairytale return for Zidane as Italy hold France at the Stade de France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0902a694f9db289bc2b9dbd36b8df7320dfb0c66a9b111077d3d9243c463def8</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:20:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261003-no-fairytale-return-for-zidane-as-italy-hold-france-at-the-stade-de-france--6174f2233f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261003-no-fairytale-return-for-zidane-as-italy-hold-france-at-the-stade-de-france" /><summary type="html">The Stade de France was filled to capacity as the new French national team manager, Zinedine Zidane, prepared to make his home debut. The very side against whom he had ended his playing career in 2006 was once again the opponent he faced. Despite Michael Olise’s splendid free kick, the French were quickly overpowered by a clinical Italian side.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's Tigray rebels abandon regional capital Mekelle as government forces enter city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e94111d409fb625613e2365085a7de34216d36682ff12ad48f66e788a106651</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T07:58:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261003-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-abandon-regional-capital-of-mekelle-as-pro-government-forces-advan--a3cb00a5f7af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261003-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-abandon-regional-capital-of-mekelle-as-pro-government-forces-advance" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian federal forces have entered the capital of the northern Tigray region and seized its airport, witnesses said Saturday, reversing a takeover by rebels from the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) that prompted the suspension of commercial flights last month. The TPLF has been fighting against pro-government forces since September 23, raising fears of an all-out civil war similar to that of 2020-2022.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 UAE investigators say Flydubai co-pilot was planning 'terrorist act'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11632bd652d36f7ec5ca0810891764d080683e86c4e5eb773dbf794e1564247d</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T07:14:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views--d42f7d08990d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes another Kyiv bridge, deepening travel chaos in Ukraine's capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96b5130b44e7caf2ceeb0a39bf3210fec5f12f395af8a07de8d5e331285a2633</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:40:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv--263369bf48e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Kyiv's Northern Bridge across the Dnipro river was hit by a Russian air attack, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said Saturday, deepening travel chaos amid an escalation in strikes ​on ‌infrastructure in the Ukrainian capital. The latest attack comes a day after the city's Southern Bridge was hit by several strikes that officials said were "tearing Kyiv apart".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UAE investigators say Omani Flydubai co-pilot was planning 'terrorist' attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d739c127e855463b146f573e4d2d0985f3a42df3623b378c696ff67c3953f9</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views--d42f7d08990d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views" /><summary type="html">The Omani co-pilot accused of attacking the captain aboard a Flydubai flight to Israel on September 30 attempted to carry out a "terrorist" attack, the United Arab Emirates prosecutor general said ​Saturday. The alleged assailant, identified as Omani national Hamam al-Hammami, had been barred from flying in his country due to his radical ideological views, several media reported.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea launches ballistic missile as tensions with Seoul grow over border mine blasts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fbcb767200062bc6f7a6c3648c8b1baa843f62b9ab84626c2fa05809300623f</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T02:40:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand--31f42c33e2e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261003-north-korea-fires-ballistic-missile-after-seoul-s-apology-demand" /><summary type="html">North Korea launched a ballistic missile Saturday morning from the Wonsan area on its east coast into the Sea of Japan, according to South Korea's military. The launch comes amid renewed tensions between Pyongyang and Seoul, with the latter demanding an apology for a blast that wounded three South Korean soldiers inside the Demilitarized Zone last month.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>French media respond to M. Le Pen’s ‘Kevlar suit’ comments against investigative outlet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9dd968bf6b2781bbfd026ebb3722196b56d9b8231a9e67559e51679011ad414</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T21:37:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261002-french-media-react-to-m-le-pen-s-kevlar-suit-comments-against-investigative-press-outlet--d4333fe88c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261002-french-media-react-to-m-le-pen-s-kevlar-suit-comments-against-investigative-press-outlet" /><summary type="html">The editorial committees of 39 French media outlets, including FRANCE 24 and RFI, on Friday released a joint statement condemning National Rally (RN) party leader and presidential candidate Marine Le Pen’s recent comments targeting investigative outlet Médiapart as “violent attempts at intimidation” against press freedom in France, qualifying them as “particularly worrying for the right to information" that citizens of a democracy "are entitled to expect”.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Nations League: France held by Italy despite Olise stunner</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a464b2c45af46f76a4f112c9de0d27762655c4d40fd85773fade32ad506b94</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T20:58:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261002-france-held-by-italy-in-zidane-s-homecoming-after-olise-stunner--929059e20009.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261002-france-held-by-italy-in-zidane-s-homecoming-after-olise-stunner" /><summary type="html">After two wins in two away games, Zinedine Zidane’s return to the Stade de France as coach was not exactly a success, as Les Bleus were held to a 1-1 draw by Italy on Friday in the UEFA Nations League.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian army pushes back Tigrayan rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0adfd49b48456b0798cf6553afc0f1bc14d45a4e2af688dbeb0da9eaeee901e</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T20:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261002-ethiopian-army-pushes-back-tigrayan-rebels--c1af64eb04a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261002-ethiopian-army-pushes-back-tigrayan-rebels" /><summary type="html">First, Ethiopia and Eritrea have severed ties and now with tensions spreading across the region, the African Union is urging all sides to show restraint. Meanwhile, Ethiopia's army is advancing toward the Tigrayan capital as fighting intensifies and new explosions rock Addis Ababa. Then, from boardrooms to cocoa fields, a growing number of urban Ivorians are turning to agriculture. On weekends, civil servants, entrepreneurs and traders leave Abidjan behind to tend farms in the countryside, seeking extra income. But running a plantation from afar comes with challenges. And, Senegal is counting down to a historic moment. In a few weeks, Dakar will host the 2026 Youth Olympic Games: the first Olympic event ever staged in Africa. But the stakes go far beyond sport. We speak to Senegal’s Minister of Sports, Djirèye Clotilde Coly.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>On the run for 20 years, Ugandan warlord Kony still 'active' within the Lord's Resistance Army</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaf7c24d7d133b2b7c01e524d93c127fefb08d9685e3653a387e09b9711463f0</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T19:31:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261002-on-the-run-for-20-years-ugandan-warlord-kony-still-active-within-the-lord-s-resistance-army--aeeee67f194b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261002-on-the-run-for-20-years-ugandan-warlord-kony-still-active-within-the-lord-s-resistance-army" /><summary type="html">In recent months, the eastern Central African Republic has been hit by several attacks attributed to the Lord’s Resistance Army (LRA), a Ugandan militia infamous for its massacres and mass abductions of children in the 1990s and 2000s. The group's leader, Joseph Kony, wanted by the International Criminal Court for more than 20 years, remains at large. FRANCE 24 spoke to Leonie von Braun, the ICC’s lead investigator on the Kony case, about the group's resurgence.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>French Unrest: Are we witnessing a new 'Yellow Vests' movement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c85a7f0e9f87526f33e8d7f34f1139e4ba4a09e3151e5134e3390e637971627a</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T18:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-french-unrest-are-we-witnessing-a-new-yellow-vests-movement--8b907c6a3cf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-french-unrest-are-we-witnessing-a-new-yellow-vests-movement" /><summary type="html">It's been 18 days since we first reported on isolated cases of schools protests at a high school in Rennes in Brittany, in Caen in Normandy and Villeneueve d'Asque on the suburbs of Lille. The complaints were similar in theme, overloaded timetables, staffing problems, poor facilities. It spread to Saint Denis and Creteil on the outskirts of Paris days later, one interview with the students was sen 1.4 million times on TikTok. It gathered pace, and morphed into what we've seen throughout the week, hundreds of protests, some peaceful, some with deeply distressing scenes, beyond the make shift barricades, a school in Nantes set off fire, firefighters forced out of the vehicle in Marseille and the fire engine set alight, scroll your socials itt's hard to miss some of the uglier scenes, a female police officer being attacked on the ground as youths shouted kill her. Where is it heading, and what has it become? Urban violence says the government, accusing agitators linked to the hard left exploiting geenuine concerns for political ends ahead of the election. Which La France Insoumise denies saying they favour no violent means of action. 
 
Today in Spotlight, we discuss this with Jean Remi Girard, a teacher in Asnieres in the north of Paris, and the President of the National Union des Lycees and Colleges, covering education workers from primary schools to college, 7 until 18.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil’s Lula gears up for ‘last dance’ with run for fourth presidential term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d491a03740ce9c5b489bdd9e3e53c849f81a2f8a51892d2a6e85136cdb3baa7</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:20:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-brazil-s-lula-gears-up-for-last-dance-with-run-for-fourth-presidential-term--5b44a3117a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-brazil-s-lula-gears-up-for-last-dance-with-run-for-fourth-presidential-term" /><summary type="html">President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will stand for re-election in Brazil on Sunday. At 80, the former steelworker hopes to capitalise on his popularity and economic successes to win a fourth term in office but is neck-and-neck in the polls with far-right rival Flavio Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'We have to close defence gaps urgently': EU Parliament Foreign Affairs Committee chief McAllister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d85fa64576d2888a37b2e264a41c48f088fc1426ca0c6656ad6d49fdf4b43bb1</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:57:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-we-have-to-close-defence-gaps-urgently-eu-parliament-foreign-affairs-committee-chief-mcalli--0a159ccef672.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-we-have-to-close-defence-gaps-urgently-eu-parliament-foreign-affairs-committee-chief-mcallister" /><summary type="html">We sit down with David McAllister, the chair of the European Parliament’s Foreign Affairs Committee. He talks to us about the security threats facing Europe, and what defence gaps the EU urgently needs to close. For McAllister, the EU is "not at war with the Russian Federation, but we are no longer at peace with Russia". He also believes that the EU is not, as yet, capable of making sovereign decisions in certain areas of defence "because we are too dependent on US capabilities."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: The craze for candidate merch ahead of elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78f2088e3039cfc0fe052bb19efffe50e7c00417630161380861118da1a078ee</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:17:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-brazil-the-craze-for-candidate-merch-ahead-of-elections--d0fbf29c88ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-brazil-the-craze-for-candidate-merch-ahead-of-elections" /><summary type="html">Nearly 159 million Brazilians will head to the polling booths on Sunday to vote in general elections. They will elect their new MPs, see two-thirds of the Senate change ranks and, most importantly, vote for their next president.Though the vote is held by secret ballot, people wear their support on their sleeve. Candidates and parties are brandished on flags throughout the streets of #RiodeJaneiro, and business is booming for vendors selling merchandise for President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his rival Flavio Bolsonaro.FRANCE 24's Brazil correspondent Jan Onoszko brings you this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spanish lawmakers vote down affordable housing bills in blow to Sanchez’s government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16ea599d5f494fa2f037587d11d02ef8957d67e7b049e615642aaff372140572</id><updated>2026-10-04T06:03:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:12:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-spanish-lawmakers-vote-down-affordable-housing-bills-in-blow-to-sanchez-s-government--f124c72c5cdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-spanish-lawmakers-vote-down-affordable-housing-bills-in-blow-to-sanchez-s-government" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators protesting against Spain's housing crisis reacted with fury on Friday after the country's parliament rejected two bills put forward by the government that centre-left Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez hoped would address their concerns. Rents have doubled over the past decade, with average prices now almost equivalent to the average young person's monthly salary.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
